", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferry_Aid", "w": 420.0, "h": 181.5, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "light-violet", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "♪ Let It Be — Ferry Aid (1987)", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Charity single after the Zeebrugge disaster, organised by The Sun, which had sold cheap tickets for that sailing."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferry_Aid", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferry_Aid", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:8GQxqi2wRCGmkuQHaSAeq", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 520.0, "y": 825.4000000000001, "rotation": 0, "index": "b2v", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dansband", "w": 420.0, "h": 157.2, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "light-violet", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "♪ Dansband — Swedish dance-band genre", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The live band in the Baltic ferry ballroom: schlager, foxtrot, matched outfits."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dansband", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dansband", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:nZIupsrvXWR2OhckqGYKA", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 980.0, "y": 849.7, "rotation": 0, "index": "b2w", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-33/chapter-I/subchapter-E/part-86/section-86.01", "w": 420.0, "h": 278.70000000000005, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "yellow", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Motif: the whistle", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ship's whistle fundamentals by length (COLREGs Annex III): 70–200 Hz for vessels ≥200 m, 130–350 Hz for 75–200 m, 250–700 Hz under 75 m; largest ships audible ~2 nm at 143 dB. Score the brand's low note in the 70–200 Hz band. — eCFR 33 CFR 86.01"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-33/chapter-I/subchapter-E/part-86/section-86.01", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-33/chapter-I/subchapter-E/part-86/section-86.01", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:p8Uvc8p0hOw3sgmX8NQrq", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 1440.0, "y": 1022.6, "rotation": 0, "index": "b2x", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foghorn", "w": 420.0, "h": 254.4, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "yellow", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Motif: the diaphone", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Robert Foulis's insight: low notes carry further. Use a two-tone diaphone 'grunt' as the transition sting. In 1982 VPRO broadcast a live foghorn concert across North Sea harbours mixed with Alvin Curran's music. — Wikipedia"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foghorn", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foghorn", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:f9cLvlB5pkNOFl2gkoFDI", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 520.0, "y": 1022.6000000000001, "rotation": 0, "index": "b2y", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://freesound.org/people/theblockofsound235/sounds/350948/", "w": 420.0, "h": 254.4, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "yellow", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Motif: the PA chime", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two- or three-note PA chime → pause → bilingual announcement. (BC Ferries' chime is C–A–F on a Roland D-50 preset, per a Freesound comment.) Build a 3-note sodium chime. — Freesound comment (anecdotal)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://freesound.org/people/theblockofsound235/sounds/350948/", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://freesound.org/people/theblockofsound235/sounds/350948/", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:T3DcZbtiLWhs0QgQXzjOt", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 60.0, "y": 1071.2, "rotation": 0, "index": "b2z", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "", "w": 420.0, "h": 181.5, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "yellow", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Motif: the bed", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Continuous diesel drone, ventilation hiss, cutlery and slot-machine bleeps far off; the hull creaks every 7–12 s with the swell."}]}]}}, "meta": {}}, {"id": "shape:ikyhxIIzXfu515VHWJhpg", "typeName": "shape", "type": "geo", "x": 980.0, "y": 1168.4, "rotation": 0, "index": "b30", "parentId": "shape:TPmHLTmtvfvTJkThUjfpF", "isLocked": false, "opacity": 1, "props": {"geo": "rectangle", "dash": "solid", "url": "https://sound-effects.bbcrewind.co.uk/07043043", "w": 420.0, "h": 254.4, "growY": 0, "scale": 1, "flipX": false, "flipY": false, "labelColor": "black", "color": "light-blue", "fill": "semi", "size": "s", "font": "sans", "align": "start", "verticalAlign": "start", "richText": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "BBC Sound Effects 07043043 — Car Ferry engine room (Sealink 'St. Nicholas', 17,400 t, built 1980)", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "RemArc licence (personal/educational/research). An actual 1980s cross-channel ferry engine room."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "https://sound-effects.bbcrewind.co.uk/07043043", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"hr